  V1 in numbers: the README's factor 1.20/0.85 is the ratio of the median factors of the two z halves (median z of the halves 0.99 and 2.19): -0.148 dex between those medians, -0.183 dex between the z < 1 and z > 2 medians; on the chart's axis (a log-linear tilt in log10 (1 + z), the change between z = 0.6 and z = 2.5) its regression tilt is -0.251 dex and the pure tilt that reproduces its flat slope is -0.241 dex.
  ratio (regression endpoint tilt) / (half-median differential) = 1.70; the same ratio for a pure log-linear tilt is 1.66 (the z baselines' ratio: 0.340 / 0.205).
